        "title": "Low Tide",
        "intro": "The following is an excerpt from a short story.",
        "text": "The two brothers had not spoken since the funeral, six years now, and the boat between them — Sam holding the tiller, Eli coiling a line he did not need to coil — carried that silence out past the breakwater like a third passenger.\n\n\"Dad would have hated this,\" Eli said finally. \"Us, not talking.\"\n\n\"Dad's not here to hate anything.\"\n\nThe boat rocked. A gull complained somewhere overhead. Eli set down the rope he'd finished coiling and started, without quite meaning to, uncoiling it again.\n\n\"I could turn us back,\" Sam said. It wasn't clear if he meant the boat.\n\nEli looked at the water, gray and moving, giving nothing away. \"Or we could just keep going out,\" he said, \"and see what's still there when we get far enough.\"\n\nNeither of them moved to change course. The shoreline behind them grew smaller. Neither of them said whether that was the plan."
