        "title": "To the Empty Chair",
        "intro": "The following is an original poem.",
        "text": "You have held your place at this table for three years now,\nnever once complaining about the dust,\nnever once asking why I set a plate\nin front of you some evenings, out of habit,\nthen quietly take it away again before dinner starts.\n\nI know you can't actually be uncomfortable.\nI know this. I say it out loud sometimes,\nlike a fact I'm still working to fully believe,\nthe way you say something true enough times\nthat it eventually stops needing to be said.\n\nYou are the most patient thing I own.\nYou do not ask when I'll finally give you away,\nor fill you again, or admit that a chair\nthat holds nothing but absence is still, somehow,\nholding something — I just haven't found the word for it yet."
