        "intro": "The following is an original poem.",
        "text": "Some mornings we wake up under clear skies,\nno warnings issued, visibility good\nfor miles in every direction we might look —\nthose are the easy days, the ones that don't\nrequire checking the forecast twice before leaving the house.\n\nOther mornings arrive already overcast,\na low front moving in from something one of us\nsaid the night before and hasn't yet apologized for,\nthe barometric pressure of the whole kitchen dropping\nthe moment the coffee finishes brewing.\n\nWe have learned, over the years, to read each other's\nsatellite imagery — the specific quality of silence\nthat means a storm is building somewhere out of sight,\nstill hours off, still possible to route around\nif one of us is willing to check the map early enough.\n\nWe have had, by now, every kind of weather\ntwo people can have together, including the days\nso still and ordinary they barely register as weather\nat all — and I have come to trust those most,\nthe unremarkable forecast, nothing severe expected, sky holding."
