        "title": "The Visitor",
        "intro": "The following is an original poem.",
        "text": "Someone knocked at the door last night. I didn't answer.\nIt might have been the wind finding the loose shutter again.\nIt might have been you, the way you used to knock —\ntwo short, one long, a code we made up young\nand never quite retired, even after we should have.\n\nI told myself it was the wind. I told myself\nthis morning, with the shutter fixed, that I was right,\nthat there was never any real question to begin with.\nI have gotten good at telling myself the version\nthat lets me sleep, and mostly, I believe the version I tell.\n\nMostly. Some nights the knocking comes back anyway,\nregardless of which story I've settled into,\nand I lie there deciding, once again, not to answer,\nnot sure anymore if I'm protecting myself from a stranger\nor from finding out, finally, that no one was ever there at all."
