        "intro": "The following is an original poem.",
        "text": "They tell the story like it's a warning about ambition —\nfly too close to the sun, the wax melts, you fall.\nMoral: know your limits. Stay reasonable. Stay low.\n\nBut nobody mentions the part where he was flying.\nNobody mentions how the wind must have felt,\nreal wind, under wings he'd never had before,\nfor however many minutes it lasted, before it didn't.\n\nI think about this more than I probably should —\nwhether I'd trade the whole cautious, sensible life\nfor those specific minutes of actual flight,\nknowing already, going in, exactly how it ends,\nthe sun, the wax, the long fall back to ordinary ground.\n\nI think, some days, I'd take the minutes anyway.\nI think Icarus knew something the warning leaves out:\nthat falling, eventually, is what happens to everyone,\nwhether or not they ever once, even briefly, flew."
