        "text": "I should tell you now, before we go any further, that I will spend a great deal of this account on the four years I spent building the company, and comparatively little on the two years after I sold it. This is not because the second period was uneventful — if anything, the opposite is true. It is because I have found, in the several previous attempts I've made to write this down, that I simply cannot make myself linger there with the same clarity I bring to everything before it. The words arrive fine enough for the building years. For what came after, they arrive thin, general, reluctant, and I have decided, finally, to stop fighting that reluctance and simply let this account reflect it honestly: four detailed years, then a handful of pages doing their best with two years I apparently am not yet capable of rendering in full."
