        "title": "The Interview",
        "intro": "The following is an excerpt from a short story.",
        "text": "Priya walked into the interview eleven minutes early, which was, obviously, exactly correct, exactly what a person who took this seriously would do, unlike whoever had scheduled the appointment before hers, who was still in there, going long, making everyone else's carefully planned morning collapse into a single undifferentiated waiting room of mounting, silent panic.\n\nShe reviewed her notes once more. Fine. They were fine. She had prepared thoroughly, more thoroughly than anyone else interviewing for this position possibly could have, and if her hands were slightly damp against the folder, that was simply the room's temperature, nothing at all to do with the fact that she'd wanted this specific job more than she'd wanted anything in years, more than felt entirely reasonable to want a job, if she was honest, which she generally tried not to be about this particular subject.\n\nThe door opened. A woman who was not the interviewer stepped out first — the previous candidate, presumably — looking so radiantly, infuriatingly confident that Priya's carefully maintained calm evaporated in roughly the time it took the woman to walk past her toward the elevator."
