        "text": "Oh, what a lovely Tuesday to lose everything —\nthe sun so bright, the birds mid-cheerful song,\nthe neighbor's children laughing at their swing,\nas if the whole bright day agreed: nothing's gone wrong.\n\nThe letter used the word 'restructuring' twice,\nand 'valued contributions' one time more,\nand wished me well, in a font almost precisely\nthe one they'd used to wish me well before,\n\nback when the news was good, back when I'd earned\nthe better kind of letter, the one with my name spelled\nin the same cheerful, corporate font, unconcerned\nwith which specific news it was asked to compel."
