        "text": "(Chapter Two, early in the novel) Wherever Yusuf saw a risk, Nadia saw an opportunity, and their partnership worked precisely because of this — his caution catching what her boldness missed, her boldness reaching what his caution would have left alone.\n\n(Chapter Twenty-Three, late in the novel) Yusuf found himself, this time, the one pushing forward, Nadia the one urging caution — neither of them entirely sure when, exactly, over these three years, they'd started trading roles, or whether they'd simply both learned something from the other they hadn't fully noticed absorbing."
