        "text": "(A long pause. Neither moves.)\n\nRENATA: I should go. Traffic.\n\nTOMAS: (not quite looking at her) Sure.\n\n(She does not move toward the car yet. He does not step back toward the house.)\n\nRENATA: I don't know what I would have said, even if I'd — even if there had been more time.\n\nTOMAS: I don't know either. I've thought about it. I don't know.\n\n(Another pause. RENATA finally moves toward her car. TOMAS does not wave, but he does not turn away either.)\n\nRENATA: (from the car, not quite a question) Same time next year? For — whatever this was?\n\nTOMAS: (a long beat) Maybe sooner.\n\n(She gets in. The car pulls away. TOMAS stands at the gate a moment longer, watching the empty road, before the lights go down.)"
