            "For full credit, also analyze the final stanza's shift from praising the hands' function to questioning 'what they cost her, or what they were, underneath all that endless doing, besides simply hands' — the poem's culminating move beyond synecdoche's reduction toward recognizing the whole person the figurative substitution had, until this point, obscured."
